{"study_accession":"PRJNA1460727","secondary_study_accession":"SRP696557","title":"Microbiome-Derived Metabolites Shape CD4⁺ T-Cell Differentiation and Immune Aging in Chronic HIV-1 Infection [RNA-Seq]","description":"The role of aromatic gut-derived bacterial metabolites (GDBMs) in shaping immune cell metabolism and function remains poorly explored. Using ex vivo metabolomic profiling of paired plasma and CD4⁺ T-cells from people living with HIV-1 (PLWH), we identified a network of aromatic GDBMs whose cell-associated abundance, rather than systemic levels, was linked to broad alterations in CD4⁺ T-cell metabolic and functional states. Among these metabolites, p- cresol sulfate (PCS) emerged as a mechanistic prototype investigated in depth. Ex vivo flow cytometry and single-cell RNA sequencing of CD4⁺ T-cells stratified by cell-associated PCS levels revealed dose-dependent enrichment of transcriptional programs associated with impaired differentiation capacity, regulatory-like identity, and cellular senescence. Consistently, in vitro transcriptomic and proteomic analyses of PCS-exposed CD4⁺ T cells demonstrated induction of cell-cycle arrest, mitochondrial dysfunction, and senescence-associated programs, including upregulation of p16 and p21. Integration of these immunometabolic features with measurements of HIV-1 reservoir size in PLWH revealed that CD4⁺ T-cell states defined by cell-associated GDBMs track with intact proviral DNA levels in vivo. Together, these findings define a microbiome-derived axis that reshapes CD4⁺ T-cell metabolism and fate and promotes immune aging–associated states in PLWH. Our data suggest that cell-associated GDBMs may foster immunometabolic CD4⁺ T-cell states previously linked to long-term HIV-1 reservoir persistence in vivo.","pubmed":"42479464;42582102","geo_series":"","n_samples":36,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN57630377","study_accession":"PRJNA1460727","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Non-proliferating CD4⁺ T-cells, 100uM PCS,HC5","description":"Non-proliferating CD4⁺ T-cells, 100uM PCS,HC5","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9709382","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-06-17","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral Blood"],["tissue","Peripheral Blood"],["cell_type","T cells"],["treatment","100uM PCS"],["group","Non-proliferating"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR38341881","experiment_accession":"SRX33176606","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":45094654,"base_count":9109120108,"first_public":"2026-06-17","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM9709382: Non-proliferating CD4⁺ T-cells, 100uM PCS,HC5 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN57630378","study_accession":"PRJNA1460727","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Proliferating CD4⁺ T-cells, 100uM PCS,HC5","description":"Proliferating CD4⁺ T-cells, 100uM PCS,HC5","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9709381","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-06-17","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral Blood"],["tissue","Peripheral Blood"],["cell_type","T cells"],["treatment","100uM PCS"],["group","Proliferating"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR38341882","experiment_accession":"SRX33176605","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":78928220,"base_count":15943500440,"first_public":"2026-06-17","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM9709381: Proliferating CD4⁺ T-cells, 100uM PCS,HC5 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN57630379","study_accession":"PRJNA1460727","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"Non-proliferating CD4⁺ T-cells, 50uM PCS,HC5","description":"Non-proliferating CD4⁺ T-cells, 50uM PCS,HC5","sex":"","geo_sample":"